        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(signal): add setup wizard",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nSignal setup needed a guided path that proves a usable receive transport before users rely on the channel, without OpenClaw creating or managing a Signal Docker container. Existing setup and status paths could also leave stale native/container transport fields ambiguous, miss account-specific API-mode behavior, or report a Signal daemon as generically working when the configured account was missing or receive was unavailable.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe Signal plugin now owns a setup wizard path for two supported transports: local `signal-cli` and an existing Signal server managed by the operator. The same change tightens native/container/auto probing so setup and status can distinguish transport reachability from account/receive readiness, and it lets multi-account Signal configs use `channels.signal.apiMode` as a channel default with per-account overrides.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers can run Signal setup, choose local `signal-cli` or an existing server URL, and have setup save config only after the selected transport is reachable for the intended account. Operators get clearer `openclaw channels status --probe` and health output for ready, account-missing, receive-unavailable, and unreachable Signal states. Existing/manual `bbernhard/signal-cli-rest-api` deployments remain supported through `apiMode: \"container\"`; OpenClaw no longer offers an OpenClaw-managed Signal Docker setup path.\n\n## Evidence\n\nBehavioral proof:\n\n- Existing-server setup prompts for a Signal account, probes the server with that account, and saves `httpUrl`, `autoStart: false`, and `apiMode: \"auto\"` after the probe succeeds.\n- Native setup clears stale external/container endpoint fields for the intended account while preserving existing custom native endpoints and channel-level `channels.signal.apiMode` defaults.\n- Container receive readiness is checked through `/v1/receive/{account}` when receive capability is required, and container account validation uses bounded `/v1/accounts` reads.\n- Signal send, reaction, monitor, attachment, and probe paths resolve account-specific `apiMode` before falling back to the channel default.\n- `openclaw channels status --probe` and health formatting expose Signal readiness states instead of reducing account-missing/receive-unavailable cases to a generic “works” signal.\n- Screenshots are omitted because this PR changes terminal/setup wizard, gateway status, config, docs, and tests rather than browser UI; command output is the reviewer-checkable proof.\n\nAutomated checks on refreshed head `86c2afa42ddce7bc42b1dc3ec5b5a5fc354de34c`:\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/signal/setup-entry.test.ts extensions/signal/src/core.test.ts extensions/signal/src/setup-core.test.ts extensions/signal/src/client-adapter.test.ts extensions/signal/src/client-container.test.ts extensions/signal/src/client.test.ts extensions/signal/src/config-schema.test.ts extensions/signal/src/install-signal-cli.test.ts extensions/signal/src/monitor.tool-result.pairs-uuid-only-senders-uuid-allowlist-entry.test.ts extensions/signal/src/send-reactions.test.ts extensions/signal/src/send.test.ts src/commands/channels.surfaces-signal-runtime-errors-channels-status-output.test.ts src/commands/health.test.ts src/plugins/official-external-plugin-catalog.test.ts` passed: 14 files across 3 Vitest shards, 403 tests.\n- `node --import tsx scripts/generate-bundled-channel-config-metadata.ts --check` passed.\n- `node --import tsx scripts/generate-config-doc-baseline.ts --check` passed after regenerating the config docs baseline on the rebased tree.\n- `node --max-old-space-size=8192 --import tsx scripts/generate-plugin-sdk-api-baseline.ts --check` passed.\n- `./node_modules/.bin/oxlint -c .oxlintrc.json extensions/signal` passed after `node scripts/prepare-extension-package-boundary-artifacts.mjs`; broad `node scripts/run-bundled-extension-oxlint.mjs` now fails on unrelated current-main Discord/Google Meet/voice-call lint findings outside this PR diff.\n- `./node_modules/.bin/oxfmt --check --threads=1 extensions/signal/src/setup-core.ts extensions/signal/src/setup-core.test.ts extensions/signal/src/core.test.ts extensions/signal/src/send-reactions.test.ts extensions/signal/src/monitor.tool-result.pairs-uuid-only-senders-uuid-allowlist-entry.test.ts && git diff --check` passed.\n- Local `pnpm` wrapper commands were blocked by an Atlassian registry 404 while fetching `@openai/codex@0.144.1`, so direct repo scripts were used for focused validation where possible; clean CI is expected to verify the full wrapper lanes on the pushed head.\n\nReview proof:\n\n- Native review phase used bare `codex review --base origin/main` and reached two consecutive clean passes on the rebased product diff.\n- Cold review phase used an isolated `codex exec` reviewer after subagent dispatch was blocked by the thread limit, and reported no concrete actionable findings.\n- Post-review fixes kept to accepted findings: three test clone calls in `extensions/signal/src/setup-core.test.ts` now use `structuredClone(...)`, and the ClawSweeper diagnostic finding is fixed by classifying configured-but-unlinked container accounts as `account_missing` while preserving `receive_unavailable` for receive endpoint failures.\n\nCI:\n\n- Awaiting fresh PR checks for pushed head `86c2afa42ddce7bc42b1dc3ec5b5a5fc354de34c`.\n\n\n\n\n",
